<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pope Pius IV</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1499">1499</a>–<a href="/years/1565">1565</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Giovanni Angelo Medici</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pius IV (1499–1565), born Giovanni Angelo Medici in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/milan">Milan</a>, was pope from 1559 to 1565. He reconvened the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/council-of-trent">Council of Trent</a> in 1562 and confirmed its decrees in 1564, completing the main programme of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/counter-reformation">Catholic Reformation</a>. His nephew <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-borromeo">Charles Borromeo</a> served as his secretary of state, and his sister Chiara's marriage into the Hohenems family brought her sons rapid advancement.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pope-pius-iv.jpg" alt="Pope Pius IV" width="320" height="418" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Circle of Scipione Pulzone · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Portrait_of_Pope_Pius_IV,_three-quarter-length,_seated_at_a_draped_table_(Circle_of_Scipione_Pulzone).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
